Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the best book from the second editions of CoD.<br /> I'm not saying this because I worked hard for it, but because everything is so awesome. Hope you like the mood of my arts.<br /> Huge compliments to everyone who worked on it.<br /> The Pure are so awesome and also the new Bale Hounds.<br /> The gifts of blood and fervor are just WOW, the Predator Kings merits are AMAZING</div> </div> </div> </div>Small shock you like the predator kings. I just read about the church. Auto kuruth just for being in the area? Jesus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T17:38:48-07:00","id":1323554,"title":"","content":"I was pretty apathetic about Werewolf's first edition; it had cool ideas but it never clicked for me. Second edition's core made me <i>respect</i> the game; it made sense to me now and had cool ideas. This book, though? It's <i>phenomenal</i> and makes me want to actually <i>play</i> it.<br /> <br /> Ghost Wolves section is the best.<br /> <br /> Great job, guys, especially the artists whom I have a lot more to say about later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T17:47:57-07:00","id":1323558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1323538#post1323538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, this is great so far. I'm just skimming through, but I especially love the stuff for the Pure. I've always been fascinated with &quot;dark mirror&quot; type enemy groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each one's also a really neat twist on their normal Tribes; Cyrus the agent of destiny, Garima the devil on your shoulder, Tejumola the mad scientist, and Mimi the born-Pure (technically a Moon-Shunned could be a Forsaken ally, but it's going to be tough getting around their genetic mission of punishing Luna for her hubris).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T18:09:26-07:00","id":1323564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1323545#post1323545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Small shock you like the predator kings. I just read about the church. Auto kuruth just for being in the area? Jesus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just auto-Kuruth. Auto-Kuruth <i>plus</i> a bunch of werewolf-worshippers following you around, dancing through the frenzy and not being murdered for it. \ud83d\ude01","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T19:38:49-07:00","id":1323586,"title":"","content":"Soooo many amazing things in this book, so many ideas.<br /> But perhaps what makes me happiest is to see the spirit occult idea I had suggested to Chris being used!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 07-10-2019, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T19:54:34-07:00","id":1323589,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna buy it and see if I don't regret it.<br /> <br /> (Not because I think it'd be bad, but my finances this month are <i>tight.)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T23:29:04-07:00","id":1323620,"title":"","content":"Quattuor is a sad dork and I love it. Just one of the many good things I have to say, more might come later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T00:31:25-07:00","id":1323625,"title":"","content":"I'm loving this book. I started reading it straight through but had a busy day so when I finished my favorites, the Bale Hounds, I began skipping around and I haven't been displeased at all (well, my only thought of something amiss was seeing the Sun Raiser without some sort of heavy attack). Even the new hosts interest me (I liked that there were new hosts in Wolfsbane, but I didn't particularly like them). Great adds all around and a lot to let sink in. Repeated mentions of black and silver, one idigam that Contagion seems to follow, whispers to werewolves to eat their own names and TFV tainting one of the Secondborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-11-2019, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T03:51:09-07:00","id":1323640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1323586#post1323586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo many amazing things in this book, so many ideas.<br /> But perhaps what makes me happiest is to see the spirit occult idea I had suggested to Chris being used!</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a fan of the original thread, and my jaw literally dropped when I saw that chapter title.<br /> <br /> Separate note - is it me or do the Void spirits seem to resemble either Acamoth or Lower Depth entities? Anyone know if that was intentional to suggest a vector for cross splat play or just a coincidence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1407,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","user":"EndlessKng","date":". 07-11-2019, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T04:13:30-07:00","id":1323641,"title":"","content":"I am exceedingly pleased with how well this book is being received. Share your thoughts on it far and wide! An RPG.net thread would be excellent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T04:35:59-07:00","id":1323643,"title":"","content":"Question about pure templates: they still get two dots of totem at character creation as it says here <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/playing-the-pure-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/playing-the-p...-the-forsaken/</a> ? Can't find this rule on Shunned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T04:46:53-07:00","id":1323644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1323643#post1323643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about pure templates: they still get two dots of totem at character creation as it says here <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://theonyxpath.com/playing-the-pure-werewolf-the-forsaken/&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/playing-the-p...-the-forsaken/</a> ? Can't find this rule on Shunned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Pure still get those two dots. It\u2019s missing from the summary page, we\u2019ll need to sort it in errata, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T06:44:01-07:00","id":1323663,"title":"","content":"Reading up on the Spirits of the Void Beyond has got me thinking-... Might the Gauntlet a terrestrial phenomenon? I mean, I wonder how far out Urfarah's death would have effected the cosmos. Maybe everything past the Moon works like it did in the Neolithic? Or in an even weirder manner? That could lead to a horrifying situation for future space explorers in the Chronicles world.<br /> <br /> I also find myself wondering about the spirits of other planets' moons-... Are they like Luna, or is she somehow special?<br /> <br /> Shadow-Space has always been an interesting thing to muse about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 07-11-2019, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T10:46:31-07:00","id":1323724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1323640#post1323640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Separate note - is it me or do the Void spirits seem to resemble either Acamoth or Lower Depth entities? Anyone know if that was intentional to suggest a vector for cross splat play or just a coincidence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, keeping in mind that acamoth represent things that are impossible to exist, the Astral Realms book does describe the far astral plane as being possibly riddled with Abyssal invasions. However, I do think that, in this case, it's just a matter of alien things from alien stars (or just space) being unable to thrive off the Essence found on Earth, which is in turn alien to them.<br /> <br /> I suppose you could say that's like a Lower Depth, with the 'it doesn't have things to sustain them' but that's true enough about space, where you lack the air to breath, water to drink, food to eat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T11:08:03-07:00","id":1323728,"title":"","content":"My first thoughts: huh, the Zurdilu remind me of my Gisilu, the difference being the methods used for their compulsion.<br /> <br /> Second.. I am in love with the Void Spirits!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T13:12:20-07:00","id":1323758,"title":"","content":"I like how Primal Form finally made it into 2e. Always liked that gift. <br /> <br /> Geryo possibly being the things that Beast's Horrors are the astral reflection of is a neat concept too. Although it's not entirely clear if the distorted growing extra heads or limbs counts as it's own mutation or is supposed to be a side effect of one of the other ones listed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T15:45:33-07:00","id":1323793,"title":"","content":"Can we talk about the hell on earth that is the Wasp Host Joining? Because that\u2019s the most disturbing thing in that book. Forget the Bale Hounds, Devourers, Geryo, Mimics, Idigam or Void Spirits( though all are fantastic), these bugs are the most existentially terrifying things in the entire book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T15:30:34-07:00","id":1324057,"title":"","content":"One question, though: I notice the Distorted lack Blood and Bone traits. While this is understandable, and there may be a rule that says they lose those traits, I don't see why they would. They're still werewolves, albeit broken ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T16:19:35-07:00","id":1324065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324057#post1324057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question, though: I notice the Distorted lack Blood and Bone traits. While this is understandable, and there may be a rule that says they lose those traits, I don't see why they would. They're still werewolves, albeit broken ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven\u2019t included Blood and Bone for any werewolf in the book. Each character has them but they\u2019re more a player thing to work for Willpower recovery. The background personalities and descriptions give info on how to run the characters as non player characters. If you want to add B&amp;B to suit your game\u2019s needs you certainly can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T16:37:20-07:00","id":1324070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1323793#post1323793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we talk about the hell on earth that is the Wasp Host Joining? Because that\u2019s the most disturbing thing in that book. Forget the Bale Hounds, Devourers, Geryo, Mimics, Idigam or Void Spirits( though all are fantastic), these bugs are the most existentially terrifying things in the entire book.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't think they're necessarily the most disturbing thing (there's a lot of that) I do think it's pretty interesting and bound to create a lot of havoc in the Hisil but also for non-Uratha creatures disturbed by that kind of stuff. Of course, it is arguably the point, as at a certain level host nests act as a sort of roach motel for humanoids.<br /> <br /> Plus it might inspire a dogooder impulse to save the person, leading to that kind of post claiming 'Can never truly be healed' life. My first werewolf came at things with a 'no killing' rule and it quickly got perverted due to the innumerable ways that things can be left wishing for that end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-12-2019, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T17:26:58-07:00","id":1324081,"title":"","content":"Also, who here loves the new Maeljin?<br /> <br /> All hail Bhal'ma, Speaker of Truth*!<br /> <br /> *&quot;Truth&quot; is a copyright of Bhal'ma, Lord of Exposure, Duke of Knowledge, He Who Whispers Weakness, Maeljin. Truth is not necessarily complete, in context, relevant, or offered when under label, and is doled out at the sufferance of Bhal'ma or his employees. Restrictions and ratings apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T17:30:51-07:00","id":1324084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324081#post1324081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, who here loves the new Maeljin?<br /> <br /> All hail Bhal'ma, Speaker of Truth*!<br /> <br /> *&amp;quot;Truth&amp;quot; is a copyright of Bhal'ma, Lord of Exposure, Duke of Knowledge, He Who Whispers Weakness, Maeljin. Truth is not necessarily complete, in context, relevant, or offered when under label, and is doled out at the sufferance of Bhal'ma or his employees. Restrictions and ratings apply.</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly kind of miss the old Maeljin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T17:37:21-07:00","id":1324085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1323793#post1323793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we talk about the hell on earth that is the Wasp Host Joining? Because that\u2019s the most disturbing thing in that book. Forget the Bale Hounds, Devourers, Geryo, Mimics, Idigam or Void Spirits( though all are fantastic), these bugs are the most existentially terrifying things in the entire book.</div> </div> </div> </div> As someone who has a fear of wasps, who was attacked by a ground wasp hive as a child I agree 2 million % <br /> <br /> Those are the scarest, most horrifying things in CoD so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T18:41:01-07:00","id":1324098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324084#post1324084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly kind of miss the old Maeljin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing stops you from using them. There\u2019s a sidebar on p.37 about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T18:57:49-07:00","id":1324102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324081#post1324081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, who here loves the new Maeljin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Me absolutely. Carnala won't be that hard to convert over, but it's great to have something more original and werewolf-oriented, while still being able to focus the interest outward. I also suspect the Church of the Wolf (another fave from the book) was created as the result of the actions of the Hounds of Exposure, as the first spark for the group occurred when witnessing a fight between two werewolves, one 'tarnished.'<br /> <br /> One possible Maeljin I was thinking of beforehand (originally an Exarch cult but the idea didn't really jibe) was one that hated the social aspect of werewolf, like the Jungle Book's 'strength of the wolf is the pack,' and instead encouraged more personal strength, with the goal of driving wolves away from social structures like packs and even tribes. It sort of fits with the Bale Hounds encouraging White Agora and taking advantage of isolated werewolves, not to mention the traps set in place for ghost wolves. Seems like the kind of thing Percupia might fit into if she took up a strength angle rather than death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-12-2019, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T19:46:16-07:00","id":1324115,"title":"","content":"I never much like the original Maeljin, and the new set are just <i>way</i> more interesting for me. Flowers of hell indeed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, previously I had thought of giving Star-Crossed four Void-Claimed Empty Wolves as a quirky miniboss squad and YOUCH that would make it a chronicles long endeavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-12-2019, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user"