actions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T23:00:11-07:00","id":1324157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324153#post1324153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Words are things.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>It was a joke about Nasuverse. The spirits of the planets taking shots at each other and Gaia possibly being an omnicidal maniac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T23:04:14-07:00","id":1324158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324157#post1324157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a joke about Nasuverse. The spirits of the planets taking shots at each other and Gaia possibly being an omnicidal maniac.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm loosely aware of the Nasuverse-the problem being that the damn thing is so big and convoluted I couldn't quite be sure what was being referenced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T04:12:09-07:00","id":1324177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324081#post1324081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, who here loves the new Maeljin?<br /> <br /> All hail Bhal'ma, Speaker of Truth*!<br /> <br /> *&quot;Truth&quot; is a copyright of Bhal'ma, Lord of Exposure, Duke of Knowledge, He Who Whispers Weakness, Maeljin. Truth is not necessarily complete, in context, relevant, or offered when under label, and is doled out at the sufferance of Bhal'ma or his employees. Restrictions and ratings apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is his TRUTH \u2122\ufe0f valid in the state of Utah though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-13-2019, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T04:56:27-07:00","id":1324184,"title":"","content":"I must say that I really like the spirits of the Void Beyond. The planetary angels are really cool, especially as they are presented as being as normal spirits as the Lunes are (which says something). Void Leviathan are truly dreadful, even if I'm a bit disappointed they are so short lived in Earth's sphere (even if it makes sense. Imagine fighting those titans in the outer space, where they have no expiration date. Now, THAT's scary). I kinda wished that this section would have got more word count, just because I love the subject. I also like the mention of Gaia and her short portrayal. <br /> <br /> As for the Void Leviathans crushing- the main thing which was strange to me was how presenting the absorption of the Leviathans into Earth's core as a bad thing, but never saying about the consequences (unless I missed something in the section). Anyway, it kind of reminds me my theory that Gaia in her early days was feeding upon the fates of many unborn worlds, and that if the Leviathans are indeed dead or stillborn Shadows of lost worlds, it could mean that Gaia is still doing so today, and Luna keeps those beasts away in order to keep Earth's spirit asleep. On the other hand, there is that theory that the reason that some whales crush upon the shore is due to lunar influence- so perhaps Luna is, in fact, the one which sends Leviathans crushing upon the world every time the Gaia moves in her sleep, out of hope that the Uratha would manage to kill the thing before it would be absorbed into her core and feed her- some sort of playing a dangerous game, but it looks like that's what Luna does since, well, ever (see the Moon Shunned for example)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T09:26:04-07:00","id":1324489,"title":"","content":"Random thought on Urinsahi, Blood of Mars. If its Bane is mineral material from Mars (which is rather hard to come by), how 'authentic' need it be? Could Mage transubstantiate some soil from Astral Mars to the Flesh and have it be effective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T11:55:42-07:00","id":1324543,"title":"","content":"I don't think so (it's not 'from' Mars). Though if you were a mage you could probably just make a weapon have the effects of a bane, I found his ban to be interesting too, I think they're purposely hard to manage due to how alien he is. That said, there are some Martian rocks on Earth, from meteorites I think. But with Urinsahi as he is, it might be easier to just try and deal with him. It's tough, and is going to poison the area to an extent, and he's very vicious, but werewolves have been killing spirits for a few years now and can probably handle him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-14-2019, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T15:59:41-07:00","id":1324568,"title":"","content":"I'm still reading the book as I'm taking my time and reading bits and pieces here and there, but man is it good material. I'd finished chapter 1 and thought the book was worth it for it alone, no matter what came after. And then it's onto granny stitches, with her wonderfully creepy art? Still 5/5 material. After being slightly disappointed by Signs of Sorcery, I am absolutely enthralled with Shunned by the Moon. Thank you to everyone who's worked on it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T16:44:30-07:00","id":1324573,"title":"","content":"If you can judge a man by the enemies they've made...<br /> <br /> What does Shunned By The Moon say about the Forsaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T17:06:06-07:00","id":1324577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324573#post1324573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can judge a man by the enemies they've made...<br /> <br /> What does Shunned By The Moon say about the Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>That they are extremely badass to even survive this long","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T21:19:51-07:00","id":1324620,"title":"","content":"Not reading still Shunned - But do book mentions the main relationship of Tribe with it's Sacred Prey? Like what makes connection between Hunters in Darkness and Host special? Or more in details of Storm Lords and Spirit-Ridden relation? Any of those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T21:46:39-07:00","id":1324628,"title":"","content":"Nah that\u2019s not what this book is about. Jesus the moon shunned though. I would love to do a moon shunned chronicle. Murder that bitch in the sky!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T01:54:01-07:00","id":1324666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324628#post1324628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah that\u2019s not what this book is about. Jesus the moon shunned though. I would love to do a moon shunned chronicle. Murder that bitch in the sky!</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m kinda meh on the Moon Shunned. On paper they are really cool, and the potential is super enticing... until you realize The gargantuan improbability Of ever even making it to the Moon, or the dangers Helios would pose, or the fact that you can\u2019t breathe on the Moon because you\u2019re only Half spirit, and the dozens of not hundreds of Idigam still locked away in Her busom... it gets less and less feasible the more one plans to do the deed.<br /> <br /> They are fantastic Lune killers, but Moon Killers they most certainly ain\u2019t. Now if the Storyteller wants to do it, none of these things are an issue, but as they are in the book.. Luna isn\u2019t going anywhere for the foreseeable future. It would be one hell of a ride and would love to see someone pull it off though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T02:19:47-07:00","id":1324671,"title":"","content":"It has just occurred to me, that I'll ever make a &quot;Mars spirits invasion&quot; game, their bane would undoubtedly be the blood of a Distorted or something Contagious like that, just so I could play a War of the Worlds scenario- tripods included. (not to mention that with Nergal's connection to the planet and his role as a plague god, I feel that I have the mythological backup for that decision).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T08:19:35-07:00","id":1324737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324666#post1324666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m kinda meh on the Moon Shunned. On paper they are really cool, and the potential is super enticing... until you realize The gargantuan improbability Of ever even making it to the Moon, or the dangers Helios would pose, or the fact that you can\u2019t breathe on the Moon because you\u2019re only Half spirit, and the dozens of not hundreds of Idigam still locked away in Her busom... it gets less and less feasible the more one plans to do the deed.<br /> <br /> They are fantastic Lune killers, but Moon Killers they most certainly ain\u2019t. Now if the Storyteller wants to do it, none of these things are an issue, but as they are in the book.. Luna isn\u2019t going anywhere for the foreseeable future. It would be one hell of a ride and would love to see someone pull it off though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, nobody said it would be easy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They'd make for good underdog protagonists.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly interested in them for the dynamic they might add to the Pure. If they were ever able to unify in any manner, they might be able to become something resembling a fourth Tribe-... And I can't be the only one who imagined Mimi being coronated by Cyrus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T08:20:16-07:00","id":1324738,"title":"","content":"Also, I just want to note that I really enjoy all the small easter eggs to Acrozatarim/ Chris Allen's previous works. Things like mentioning Hong Kong's strange Change stealing phenomenon or the argent ghoul in reference to the Cull are really awesome (it actually made me to re-read Five Pounds of Meat for the last one). Also, all the short references for the Eater of Names, Gaia and Sea are all cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T08:47:46-07:00","id":1324744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324738#post1324738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I just want to note that I really enjoy all the small easter eggs to Acrozatarim/ Chris Allen's previous works. Things like mentioning Hong Kong's strange Change stealing phenomenon or the argent ghoul in reference to the Cull are really awesome (it actually made me to re-read Five Pounds of Meat for the last one). Also, all the short references for the Eater of Names, Gaia and Sea are all cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t forget his Lycaon-Ur references in the Devourer\u2019s section","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T10:00:03-07:00","id":1324757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324744#post1324744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don\u2019t forget his Lycaon-Ur references in the Devourer\u2019s section</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering if the devourers were related to that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T15:58:35-07:00","id":1324826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324757#post1324757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was wondering if the devourers were related to that!</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m assuming so, seeing as many of their Enlightenments are identical to Lycaon-Urs special powers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T05:18:22-07:00","id":1324938,"title":"","content":"What happens to the Moon gifts of someone that undertook the Flay Auspice rite: reimbursed experience or still usable?<br /> <br /> Do Void Reavers recoup the experience of Moon gifts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T05:43:37-07:00","id":1324945,"title":"","content":"If you\u2019ve just got the singular Moon Gift you haven\u2019t paid experience for it (you buy Renown, not Moon Gift) and personally I wouldn\u2019t reimburse anything. And if you lose your auspice I wouldn\u2019t allow continued use of Moon Gifts. As for Void Reivers, I\u2019d say not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T06:40:10-07:00","id":1324953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324577#post1324577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That they are extremely badass to even survive this long</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and by sheer virtue of biology they are the most superior species on the planet, the badassery only acts as a force multiplier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T08:39:49-07:00","id":1324972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324184#post1324184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that I really like the spirits of the Void Beyond. The planetary angels are really cool, especially as they are presented as being as normal spirits as the Lunes are (which says something). Void Leviathan are truly dreadful, even if I'm a bit disappointed they are so short lived in Earth's sphere (even if it makes sense. Imagine fighting those titans in the outer space, where they have no expiration date. Now, THAT's scary). I kinda wished that this section would have got more word count, just because I love the subject. I also like the mention of Gaia and her short portrayal.<br /> <br /> As for the Void Leviathans crushing- the main thing which was strange to me was how presenting the absorption of the Leviathans into Earth's core as a bad thing, but never saying about the consequences (unless I missed something in the section). Anyway, it kind of reminds me my theory that Gaia in her early days was feeding upon the fates of many unborn worlds, and that if the Leviathans are indeed dead or stillborn Shadows of lost worlds, it could mean that Gaia is still doing so today, and Luna keeps those beasts away in order to keep Earth's spirit asleep. On the other hand, there is that theory that the reason that some whales crush upon the shore is due to lunar influence- so perhaps Luna is, in fact, the one which sends Leviathans crushing upon the world every time the Gaia moves in her sleep, out of hope that the Uratha would manage to kill the thing before it would be absorbed into her core and feed her- some sort of playing a dangerous game, but it looks like that's what Luna does since, well, ever (see the Moon Shunned for example)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't have the book yet (but will soon). Just tell me: is there reference to Luna as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theia_(planet)\" target=\"_blank\">Theia</a>?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T22:00:05-07:00","id":1325151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1324972#post1324972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't have the book yet (but will soon). Just tell me: is there reference to Luna as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theia_(planet)\" target=\"_blank\">Theia</a>?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>No reference, but it's definitely something that I found myself thinking about when reading that section.<br /> <br /> Y'know, actually, I recall something about Theia being mentioned in some First Edition book, but I can't remember which one it was. Can anyone else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 07-17-2019, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T22:15:00-07:00","id":1325152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1325151#post1325151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know, actually, I recall something about Theia being mentioned in some First Edition book, but I can't remember which one it was. Can anyone else?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the name of an Ivory Claw in <i>The Pure</i> with a particular fascination for Luna's history; notably, her pack's totem is a Lune-Helion magath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T12:26:47-07:00","id":1325355,"title":"","content":"It's also connected (albeit unofficially) with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1174969-six-pups-a-changing?p=1175765#post1175765\">Acrozatarim's Envoys</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T13:21:51-07:00","id":1325380,"title":"","content":"So much good stuff in this book! I have a habit of overwriting things, getting bored halfway through and giving up. So I'm going to try and power through some quick points so that I might actually contribute something for a change...<ul><li>The Pure stuff is fantastic. It's a great glimpse into the culture of these enemies, and it (for lack of a better term) humanizes them without making them less villainous. The Pure definitely are dangerous, cruel and frequently evil, while still being people with a believable world view. Given the universe of dog-eat-dog savagery they live in, you can see how radicalizing like they have might appeal to some. And why many would reject the Forsaken's message of guilt and burden; why should <i>we </i>suffer and die for the actions of people who died ages ago? <i>I</i> didn't kill Father Wolf. Combined with the very flavorful tribes, that's a pretty cool package.</li> <li>Bale Hounds are great. A really interesting new flavor on the relationship between werewolves and spirits. I like the idea that barely anyone, even the Bale Hounds themselves, even know what they're <i>really </i>serving. And the insidious way the Maeljin worm their way into a werewolf's life, and basically set them on a slippery slope that's almost impossible to escape...it could make for some very interesting Chronicles, even setting aside the obvious &quot;there's a traitor in our midst&quot; plot.</li> <li>All the new Hosts are creepy and great. I like the variety they offer; some are entrenched in positions that make a head-on attack difficult, so you'd have to come at them from a different way. The Wasp Host definitely was written with her skyscraper as a playground for the pack to fight up through.</li> <li>The Void Spirits offer a fascinating expansion of the cosmology of the Shadow. &quot;Are there spirits beyond Earth?&quot; is a question I've seen a lot, and the answer here, such as it is, is a great one. There are...but they're <i>really weird</i>. I especially like the gradation, where you can do anything from an isolated monster of the week (&quot;Huh, that was a weird spirit we fought, right guys?&quot;) to a full-on &quot;alien&quot; invasion storyline.</li> <li>Mimics, huh? Not sure what to make of these. At the very least, they're something interesting to toss at a pack that thinks it has a good bead on things. Remind them there's more in Earth and Shadow than they know.</li> <li>Always nice to see a reminder that humanity can pack a punch in RD-13. Humans have been figuring out how to beat stuff that seems out of their league for thousands of years, and honestly I'd bet on humanity as a whole against any splat in the <i>CofD</i>, really. The darkness-dwellers may have secrets and power, and may see humans as weak and stupid, but there's a <i>reason </i>they have to stick to the shadows.</li> <li>More idigam are great, and the Geryo are another cool &quot;monster's monster&quot; to go up against.</li> </ul>For now, I'll just end with saying how impressed I am with the sheer variety of enemies there are. It makes sense, given that <i>Forsaken </i>is &quot;the game where you hunt things,&quot; so you'd want quite a lot of targets with very different hunts necessary to take down. What's great is that all of them flow quite naturally from the strong core premise of the game, but show how you can take it in very different directions. From gang wars with the Pure, to spy thrillers with the Bale Hounds and kaiju fights against the geryo, it's all just...awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T15:33:32-07:00","id":1325752,"title":"","content":"Got the book, so started to read it - unexpectedly, from Chapter Six <i>'Commencing the Hunt'</i>. Chapter is great introduction to <b>WtF</b> 2E setting and all - but it's <i>really </i>weird it's last chapter. ( At least in Advanced PDF version.) <i>'Commencing'</i> gives all the context various antagonists of the book to be used - and advice you what baddies you want to use in what game scenario.<br /> <br /> I really like chronicles ideas in <i>'A Hunt for Everyone'</i> subchapter - it really shows about what the <b>WtF</b> stories can be. In simple list - that is detailed, expanded and pointed what antagonists to use - are those stories concepts:<br /> * Defending your's pack territory<br /> * Negotiating Protectorate between packs<br /> * New pack get\u2019s territory after old pack disappeared.<br /> * Pack chosen by Luna<br /> * Apocalypse after Pure restore Pangea<br /> * Wolf-Blooded and human pack members fixing problems made by Urathas.<br /> <br /> It really is <b>WtF</b> as game as stories, in nutshell. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-19-2019, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T15:50:19-07:00","id":1325758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1325752#post1325752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got the book, so started to read it - unexpectedly, from Chapter Six 'Commencing the Hunt'. Chapter is great introduction to WtF 2E setting and all - but it's really weird it's last chapter. ( At least in Advanced PDF version.) 'Commencing' gives all the context various antagonists of the book to be used - and advice you what badies you want to use in what game scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably since this is a Night Horrors book, the decision was made to put the horrors front and centre and the Storyteller advice in the back. The entire thing is awesome anyhow!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T17:37:57-07:00","id":1325796,"title":"","content":"^^^<br /> <br /> This. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T21:10:35-07:00","id":1325862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1325380#post1325380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Void Spirits offer a fascinating expansion of the cosmology of the Shadow. &quot;Are there spirits beyond Earth?&quot; is a question I've seen a lot, and the answer here, such as it is, is a great one. There are...but they're <i>really weird</i>. I especially like the gradation, where you can do anything from an isolated monster of the week (&quot;Huh, that was a weird spirit we fought, right guys?&quot;) to a full-on &quot;alien&quot; invasion storyline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading people's reactions to Void Spirits... all I can say is... man. Neon Genesis Evangelion got awfully furry.<br /> <br /> (Also, yeah, I echo everyone's positive sentiments about the book, but nothing to add.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T22:26:59-07:00","id":1325878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1323663#post1323663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading up on the Spirits of the Void Beyond has got me thinking-... Might the Gauntlet a terrestrial phenomenon? I mean, I wonder how far out Urfarah's death would have effected the cosmos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider, for a moment, nobody can hear you howl in space.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T22:40:11-07:00","id":1325881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1325758#post1325758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably since this is a Night Horrors book, the decision was made to put the horrors front and centre and the Storyteller advice in the back. The entire thing is awesome anyhow!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still a bit <i>strange</i>, as horrors and antagonists are used and chosen by Storyteller. Players do not use those, only ST does. So Storytelling chapter on start of book, putting antagonists in book in context is in order, in my POV. It's like '<i>if you are Storyteller, you can do this things with <b>WtF</b></i> - and for that choose antagonist A, B or C we showing in this book, on pages X, Y or Z'.<br /> <br /> It's not something I will fight for - it's just it's <i>really</i> strange to read it that way - and it will be much more confusing for new Storytellers this section is primed for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-19-2019, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T22:49:49-07:00","id":1325885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1325862#post1325862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading people's reactions to Void Spirits... all I can say is... man. Neon Genesis Evangelion got awfully furry.<br /> <br /> (Also, yeah, I echo everyone's positive sentiments about the book, but nothing to add.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Void Spirits lit a fire in my brain as a starting point for a Chronicle. The idea basically being a Void Spirit having been bound in the territory of a pack long ago, and after that pack as passed, the spirit totem of that pack hunts down the descendants of the original pack to bring them back together because the binding on the Void Spirit is threatening to break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T22:54:37-07:00","id":1325888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1325881#post1325881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's still a bit strange, as horrors and antagonists are used and chosen by Storyteller. Players do not use those. So Storytelling chapter, putting antagonists in book in context, is in order, in my POV. It's like 'if you are Storyteller, you can do this things with WtF - and for that choose antagonist A, B or C we showing in this book, on pages X, Y or Z'.<br /> <br /> It's not something I will fight for - it's just it's really strange to read it that way - and it will be much more confusing for new Storytellers this section is primed for.</div> </div> </div> </div>... I think that would turn a lot of people off. Like, what your describing has a logic to it and I totally get that\u2019s your preference (which you are entitled to), but if I were a new storyteller and the monster book started with an essay, I\u2019d probably put it back on the shelf. <br /> <br /> Contrast with when I first picked up the monster manual, flipped through and thought \u201cI have no idea what this means, but damn those monsters and snippets I\u2019ve read are awesome!\u201d And that is what got my into RPGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T01:01:00-07:00","id":1325905,"title":"","content":"Reading subchapter about Pure, I'm surprised they do not have ANY modifications to Harmony rules. I would envision that at least few Breaking Points would be different in Oaths of Urfarah - based on Pure book from 1E line...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T07:50:53-07:00","id":1325983,"title":"","content":"Some thoughts on the werewolf foes.<br /> <br /> -Aishah is a good example of a Bale Hound. Not some gibbering cultist, not some corrupted person. A lonely girl who changed and then found her ONLY solace in a poisonous friend who listened. Her story has a lot of meaning.<br /> <br /> -I love the how the Pure NPCs are so varied not just by race or breaking the tribal molds, but also showcasing minor modifications in the uratha. Tejumola being an Ivory Claw is such a great showcase of the tribe not being a WASP hive.<br /> <br /> -Oh man the Ghost Wolves. I love the tyrants so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T10:04:26-07:00","id":1326025,"title":"","content":"Quattuor is an adorable derp, especially its accidental rise to internet fame. I just imagine it just standing there all baffled until it disappeared.<br /> <br /> The Geryo are pretty neat, there is a clear sense that they are still people despite being monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T11:51:53-07:00","id":1326053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1325355#post1325355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also connected (albeit unofficially) with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1174969-six-pups-a-changing?p=1175765#post1175765\">Acrozatarim's Envoys</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aha! Thanks! I had forgotten that one. God those are horrible creatures of cyclopean ruin. I'm picturing Dormammu at work and looking forward to using one at some point.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T13:11:45-07:00","id":1326082,"title":"","content":"I think it was a good choice to not mention every point of the oath to Urfarah. Mainly because the Pure book from first ed is one of the best, maybe the best, book of the old edition.<br /> I still use it, like lore of the forsaken and blood of the wolf. <br /> <br /> By the way, let's celebrate with some colors.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://scontent-cdt1-1.xx.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/67413736_130025211568260_1532590806777462784_n.jpg?_nc_cat=105&amp;_nc_oc=AQm4VEaxeCK5S8H0deaPhcIE_hw04iPsATTY79yJBdo0kLxuR7Vr6uyAF5yb0Xau8q8&amp;_nc_ht=scontent-cdt1-1.xx&amp;oh=672b4aacd56bb8845dd71d208cb6050c&amp;oe=5DB7CD10\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T15:24:53-07:00","id":1326116,"title":"","content":"Can you do a collage with the biker Uratha and another with the fancy pants Uratha? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3773_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3773\" data-vbnamecard=\"3773\">Helur</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T20:19:12-07:00","id":1326171,"title":"","content":"just wondering, its said the older and more corrupt (tarnished to corrupted to defiled) a bale hound gets, the more utterly disgusting both spiritually and physically. but to me at least, it seems the Lobbyist is much more disgusting in his physical wolf appearance than the lying tongue Defiled Bale Hound. am I just misunderstanding how the corruption works?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T20:53:43-07:00","id":1326178,"title":"","content":"Tejumola is my waifu. Nigerian badass mad scientist Ivory Claw, what's not to love?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T21:52:03-07:00","id":1326196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326171#post1326171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">just wondering, its said the older and more corrupt (tarnished to corrupted to defiled) a bale hound gets, the more utterly disgusting both spiritually and physically. but to me at least, it seems the Lobbyist is much more disgusting in his physical wolf appearance than the lying tongue Defiled Bale Hound. am I just misunderstanding how the corruption works?</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Bale Hound is unique. Rules are rules in an out of character context, but in character things progress as the description and imagination requires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T22:36:20-07:00","id":1326201,"title":"","content":"Werewolf 2e is my groups favorite PnP game.. by a wide margin. We - I specifically as ST - have been chomping at the bit waiting for this book. And here it is.. and it's AWESOME!<br /> <br /> Love the Night Horror series and this is one of the best yet!<br /> <br /> HAAAWWWOOOOOO!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T23:50:58-07:00","id":1326206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326082#post1326082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it was a good choice to not mention every point of the oath to Urfarah. Mainly because the Pure book from first ed is one of the best, maybe the best, book of the old edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there is a difference between <i>'Pure characters have different Breaking Point that we not mention in this book' </i>you think it is and literal quote of the <b>Shunned by the Moon</b> on their Harmony rules :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SbtM, p.14</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure suffer just as the Forsaken do when going against the dictates of their nature; violating the Oath of the Moon is a breaking point for the Pure as well, even if they choose to call it the Oath of Urfarah.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Pure have the same Breaking Points of Harmony as Forsaken in 2E rules -&gt;<br /> So the Pure are under those Breaking Points also:<ul><li><i>Imru Nu Fir Imru \u2014 </i>The People Do Not Murder The People</li> <li><i>Ni Daha \u2014 </i>Respect Your Prey</li> <li><i>Uratha Safal Thil Lu\u2019u \u2014 </i>The Uratha Shall Cleave To The Human</li> <li><i>Nu Hu Uzu Eren \u2014 </i>Do Not Eat The Flesh Of Man Or Wolf</li> </ul>Which are in direct opposition of rules that shown are for Oaths of <i>Urfarah</i> shown in <b>The Pure</b> 1E book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>To show difference - in 1E Pure book particular Oath is stated </b><i>'Pure do not murder Pure'</i><b> - and it's changes </b><i>everything</i><b> in killing rules of Forsaken for Pure characters. </b>Old book goes on lengths stating it means that Pure can freely kill Forsaken and Ghost Wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-20-2019, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T00:33:29-07:00","id":1326208,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, I'm kind of confused there as well... There seems to be a point of contradiction between the 2E Core and Shunned by the Moon.<br /> <br /> 2E Core - page 104 under Harmony in the sidebar &quot;Breaking Points&quot; - has the line &quot;Violating the Oath of the Moon. (Forsaken only, -2)&quot;<br /> <br /> Shunned by the Moon - page 14 under Tribal Bans and Oaths - has the line &quot;The Pure suffer just as the Forsaken do when going against the dictates of their nature; violating the Oath of the Moon is a breaking point for the Pure as well, even if they choose to call it the Oath of Urfarah.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is my thinking about this wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T00:59:21-07:00","id":1326209,"title":"","content":"Possibly. To read it another way, we\u2019re just saving ourselves from writing a new line in the Harmony table that says \u201cViolating the Oath of Urfarah. (Pure only, -2)\u201d<br /> <br /> Achieves the same result, and though there\u2019s some difference in nuance, essentially what the werewolves like to view as a code is actually part of their nature.<br /> <br /> In truth, the table should add a third line saying (in facetious terms) \u201cViolating either Oath even though you never swore it. (Ghost Wolves only, -2)\u201d, because Harmony is part of Uratha nature, not a lifestyle choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T01:08:23-07:00","id":1326212,"title":"","content":"Could we simply get clearer defintion on Pure 2E Harmony, stating 'it's mechanicly work the same as Forsaken, only Breaking Points can be different ( see The Pure book from 1E)' - or something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T01:30:35-07:00","id":1326216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326209#post1326209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly. To read it another way, we\u2019re just saving ourselves from writing a new line in the Harmony table that says \u201cViolating the Oath of Urfarah. (Pure only, -2)\u201d<br /> <br /> Achieves the same result, and though there\u2019s some difference in nuance, essentially what the werewolves like to view as a code is actually part of their nature.<br /> <br /> In truth, the table should add a third line saying (in facetious terms) \u201cViolating either Oath even though you never swore it. (Ghost Wolves only, -2)\u201d, because Harmony is part of Uratha nature, not a lifestyle choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm... I think to make it simpler for myself... I'm just gonna run with the Oath of the Moon applies to all Uratha, and while the Pure follow something similar that they call the Oath of Urfarah, the differences they want to exist don't actually apply and they'll still suffer breaking points when they run afoul of them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T01:56:51-07:00","id":1326218,"title":"","content":"So Oaths of Urfarah do not have any mechanical difference from Oaths of Moon? Cause it have real game world repercussions. That would meant that Pure are going quickly to Z'iir levels ( Harmony 0) simply from that they hunt Forsaken, dominate or torture humans and do every bidding of spirit lords. And this not the picture I have reading example NPC in Shunned by the Moon...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T02:12:52-07:00","id":1326221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326218#post1326218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Oaths of Urfarah do not have any mechanical difference from Oaths of Moon? Cause it have real game world repercussions. That would meant that Pure are going quickly to Z'iir levels ( Harmony 0) simply from that they hunt Forsaken, dominate or torture humans and do every bidding of spirit lords. And this not the picture I have reading example NPC in Shunned by the Moon...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think hunting Forsaken breaks any Oaths... If that was the case, Blood Talons would be in a lot of trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T02:26:32-07:00","id":1326223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326218#post1326218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Oaths of Urfarah do not have any mechanical difference from Oaths of Moon? Cause it have real game world repercussions. That would meant that Pure are going quickly to Z'iir levels ( Harmony 0) simply from that they hunt Forsaken, dominate or torture humans and do every bidding of spirit lords. And this not the picture I have reading example NPC in Shunned by the Moon...</div> </div> </div> </div>Even in 1st Edition killing an Uratha was a sin against Harmony.<br /> <br /> The Pure page 33:<br /> &quot;In seeing the Forsaken as lesser, the Pure theoretically believe it\u2019s perfectly acceptable to murder the Forsaken. Not just to kill in the heat of battle \u2014 but to outright execute them. (Note that this still constitutes a Harmony violation. The Oath to Urfarah and sins against nature are not in accord.) In fact, some grudgingly accept that murdering Forsaken is the only way that Pangaea and Fa-ther Wolf will be allowed to return. Still, killing Forsaken rattles many Pure, whether or not they admit it out loud.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T02:41:41-07:00","id":1326225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326216#post1326216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hrm... I think to make it simpler for myself... I'm just gonna run with the Oath of the Moon applies to all Uratha, and while the Pure follow something similar that they call the Oath of Urfarah, the differences they want to exist don't actually apply and they'll still suffer breaking points when they run afoul of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There you go <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>, that\u2019s the simple version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T02:57:04-07:00","id":1326227,"title":"","content":"If you want an official clarification, Paradim has the right of it. The particular clarification on the Oath of the Moon and the Pure in Shunned is my work, and it is absolutely my intent that it work that way.<br /> <br /> The Oath of the Moon is a codification of various transgressions that are spiritually corrosive for Uratha. It doesn't matter if the Pure tell themselves that killing werewolves is fine if they're Forsaken, it's still spiritually corrosive for them to do so, much as it is for Forsaken to kill Pure. The Pure don't get an out just because they want it to be otherwise.<br /> <br /> You'll note that in 1st edition, the Pure had <i>massive problems</i> with their Harmony and had all manner of methods around scouring themselves of the sins <i>they knew they were committing</i>, attempting to balance what they were doing, and so forth. The same is true in 2nd edition, except it's a more inherent part of werewolf existence - being an Uratha means you're always having to struggle with the two sides of Harmony, and it's (broadly speaking) easier to rectify that balance simply through purposeful or instinctive action.<br /> <br /> The Pure have never had a spiritual free pass for murdering or torturing Forsaken. Some of them lie to themselves that they do. The honest ones know they don't, and either don't care, or try to mitigate or repent for it because they believe it's a necessity.<br /> <br /> Honestly that one throwaway line in the 2nd ed core that the Oath of the Moon Harmony breaks are only for Forsaken is very unfortunate, because it's essentially incorrect, and we could honestly do with a slightly revised write-up of how Harmony works to adjust for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T03:27:54-07:00","id":1326232,"title":"","content":"I'll be honest, the whole 'Pure are subject to Harmony' in 1st ed was one of my least favourite aspects of it. I don't like the idea that the antagonist faction is literally shown to be wrong through the morality stat, it removed a lot of vagueness from the conflict. The idea that the other werewolves are rejecting the moon outright was cool and the idea that they MIGHT have a point was good fodder for ambiguity.<br /> <br /> The new Harmony being more fluid, it is easier to accept and less clear on who is in the right.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, the Pure do TERRIBLE things and I'm not here to discount -that-, just that I enjoy there being a sense of 'what if' about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T04:06:23-07:00","id":1326236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326227#post1326227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The particular clarification on the Oath of the Moon and the Pure in Shunned is my work, and it is absolutely my intent that it work that way. ( and rest of it )</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I see it's not the writing omission. I see how you wanted to fix the Harmony rules for 2E gameline - and I accept that. Only if we go with this new paradigm - should not Pure get small bonuses for the Breaking Points on their own interpretations for Oaths of <i>Urfarah</i>? If traditionalist Pure are following 'Pure do not kill Pure' ( based from 1E book ) - should they not get +1 bonus to killing Forsaken, as their Tribes code is pointing to this actions? So traditionalist Pure would have -1 Breaking Points, in the end ( -2 from Oaths/physical breaking, +1 for following their reinterpretation in <i>Urfarahs</i> Oaths ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T04:11:16-07:00","id":1326237,"title":"","content":"No. You\u2019re missing the point. No matter that they dress it up as \u2018oaths\u2019 these factors are inherent to the Uratha condition. Harmony doesn\u2019t care that you have interpretations, you\u2019re still going against your inner nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T04:15:18-07:00","id":1326238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326221#post1326221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think hunting Forsaken breaks any Oaths... If that was the case, Blood Talons would be in a lot of trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, <i>it <b>is </b>Harmony problem </i>for Blood Talons to kill Pure and other Uratha. Even it's pointed in Tribe write-up in 2E corebook -<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2E, p. 35</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Blood Talons have an element of the unnatural about them, one that makes the other tribes uneasy. Apex predators aren\u2019t supposed to hunt their own: The tiger doesn\u2019t eat the tiger, and the great white shark leaves other great whites alone. <br /> The <i>Suthar Anzuth</i> make a conscious decision to buck that trend, to prey on their own blood kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Elodoths archetype from Blood Talons -<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2E, p. 22</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Blood Talons</b>: The half-moons of the Blood Talons are experts in exceptions to the Oath of the Moon. After all, the Oath says <i>Imru nu fir Imru</i>: The People do not kill the People. But the People clearly do kill the People, and that means the Oath must allow for that under certain conditions. The Blood Talon Elodoth, then, is the werewolf who passes judgment on other werewolves, condemning them to die \u2014 and reassuring her tribemates that carrying out that sentence is just.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T04:24:42-07:00","id":1326239,"title":"","content":"Wyrd, Paradim didn\u2019t say kill. They said hunt. There\u2019s no issue with werewolves hunting other werewolves, and we\u2019ve spent considerable words explaining that hunts don\u2019t always end in death.<br /> <br /> I would greatly appreciate it if you\u2019d spend more time reading what people actually say, and less time weaponising book quotes against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T04:25:25-07:00","id":1326240,"title":"","content":"Reading Geyro section, I like how developers took general idea of '<i>ancient evil, something like Idigam - but based on myths</i>' - like my own <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1137943-2e-fear-of-scales-%E2%80%93-dragon-idigam\"><b>Fear of Scales</b></a> - and made some new Prey category that is much more fitting to the shown idea, than Idigam as direct antagonists template. In free time, I will change <i>Fear of Scales</i> write-up to that of Geyro, as it's much more fitting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-20-2019, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T05:06:24-07:00","id":1326244,"title":"","content":"<b>Geryo</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326232#post1326232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be honest, the whole 'Pure are subject to Harmony' in 1st ed was one of my least favourite aspects of it. I don't like the idea that the antagonist faction is literally shown to be wrong through the morality stat, it removed a lot of vagueness from the conflict. The idea that the other werewolves are rejecting the moon outright was cool and the idea that they MIGHT have a point was good fodder for ambiguity.<br /> <br /> The new Harmony being more fluid, it is easier to accept and less clear on who is in the right.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, the Pure do TERRIBLE things and I'm not here to discount -that-, just that I enjoy there being a sense of 'what if' about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What is better - to be born good, or to overcome your evil nature through great effort?&quot;<br /> - Paarthurnax, Skyrim<br /> <br /> Harmony is about adhering to the innate nature of the Uratha, not about who's right or wrong. Remember that Kuruth is also part of the Uratha's nature, and it can easily lead to the death of innocents, pack mates and loved ones, for the &quot;crime&quot; of happen to be nearby.<br /> Sacrificing your Harmony for your beliefs is actually quite noble. It'll be punishing, but you take the punishment for what you think is right.<br /> Is avenging Urfarah's death right? Well, the Pure think so, and they are willing to go against their nature for the sake of justice. (By which I mean their sense of justice, not mine.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T05:51:21-07:00","id":1326247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326244#post1326244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Geryo</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;What is better - to be born good, or to overcome your evil nature through great effort?&quot;<br /> - Paarthurnax, Skyrim<br /> <br /> Harmony is about adhering to the innate nature of the Uratha, not about who's right or wrong. Remember that Kuruth is also part of the Uratha's nature, and it can easily lead to the death of innocents, pack mates and loved ones, for the &quot;crime&quot; of happen to be nearby.<br /> Sacrificing your Harmony for your beliefs is actually quite noble. It'll be punishing, but you take the punishment for what you think is right.<br /> Is avenging Urfarah's death right? Well, the Pure think so, and they are willing to go against their nature for the sake of justice. (By which I mean their sense of justice, not mine.)</div> </div> </div> </div>OOCly, Uratha are still the main player characters and the Pure are presented as their foes. That was the mentality I used when I thought about this.<br /> <br /> But yeah, if you spin it the way you did, absolutely Pure can be seen as noble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T07:06:58-07:00","id":1326257,"title":"","content":"They're still presented as the antagonists. I merely pointed out that Harmony is a measure of how well Uratha align with their nature, and not a measure of how right they are and how good it is to follow their nature. From there it's all about how you frame the conflict and the justifications of both sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T08:17:20-07:00","id":1326264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326247#post1326247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OOCly, Uratha are still the main player characters and the Pure are presented as their foes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Small nitpick, but crucial to Harmony rules talk - <i>Uratha</i> is name for <b>all</b> human-wolf spirit hybrids, i.e. werewolves race - Forsaken, Pure or Ghost Wolves, all of them. PCs in game are pointed to be more Forsaken, maybe Ghost Wolves - Pure are clearly antagonists of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T08:20:51-07:00","id":1326267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326221#post1326221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think hunting Forsaken breaks any Oaths... If that was the case, Blood Talons would be in a lot of trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even Sacred Hunts require the prey to die.<br /> <br /> If killing Uratha is spiritually corrosive, imagine how corrosive it was to kill Urfarah. The Pure simply misguidedly butcher Forsaken in a feeble attempt to balance a long defunct karmic wheel. And it won't work for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 07-20-2019, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T08:41:32-07:00","id":1326273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326196#post1326196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every Bale Hound is unique. Rules are rules in an out of character context, but in character things progress as the description and imagination requires.</div> </div> </div> </div>ahh ok I understand. thanks for the explanation!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T08:53:42-07:00","id":1326279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326267#post1326267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not even Sacred Hunts require the prey to die.<br /> <br /> If killing Uratha is spiritually corrosive, imagine how corrosive it was to kill Urfarah. The Pure simply misguidedly butcher Forsaken in a feeble attempt to balance a long defunct karmic wheel. And it won't work for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building on this, I'm fond of that old bit of lore which says Urfarah's death site is a really nasty Wound because of the sheer amount of spiritual corrosion the act of killing Father Wolf caused. I think (not near my books) the place was Thurifuge's den, and Thurifuge was BIG in 1E terms (I used to call him &quot;Chronicles of Darkness' Khorne&quot;, for those versed with Warhammer), but it's an aspect of the setting that carries out easily into 2E without having to involve it or other specific Maeljin.<br /> <br /> While I'm at it, how cool and, most importantly, relevant and dangerous for Forsaken and Pure are the new Maeljin? Because earlier ones were not bad, but they sorta were &quot;Seven Sins and then some, might cross a werewolf path because temptation and bad people&quot;. These? These are a scourge for <i>every single werewolf</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 07-20-2019, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T09:10:31-07:00","id":1326283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326279#post1326279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Building on this, I'm fond of that old bit of lore which says Urfarah's death site is a really nasty Wound because of the sheer amount of spiritual corrosion the act of killing Father Wolf caused. I think (not near my books) the place was Thurifuge's den, and Thurifuge was BIG in 1E terms (I used to call him &quot;Chronicles of Darkness' Khorne&quot;, for those versed with Warhammer), but it's an aspect of the setting that carries out easily into 2E without having to involve it or other specific Maeljin.<br /> <br /> While I'm at it, how cool and, most importantly, relevant and dangerous for Forsaken and Pure are the new Maeljin? Because earlier ones were not bad, but they sorta were &quot;Seven Sins and then some, might cross a werewolf path because temptation and bad people&quot;. These? These are a scourge for <i>every single werewolf</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) It was said to be the First Wound.<br /> <br /> 2) The Khorne of CofD would be Asmodai who wants blood for blood's sake, Thurifuge is the Architect of Violence. The one who feeds from institutionalized violence, the one who feed from the engineering act that was the so called Final Solution, or the infrastructure put forward in the prosecution of wars.<br /> <br /> The thing about the Maeljin is, they have dozens of names. Could easily slap Pseulak into Shad'ma; or Baalphegor into Lakh'ma, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T11:45:34-07:00","id":1326311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326267#post1326267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not even Sacred Hunts require the prey to die.<br /> <br /> If killing Uratha is spiritually corrosive, imagine how corrosive it was to kill Urfarah. The Pure simply misguidedly butcher Forsaken in a feeble attempt to balance a long defunct karmic wheel. And it won't work for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not all Pure do. Even the 2E Core points out that there are some Pure who see murdering Forsaken as a wrong to be avoided. For example, take the perspective that every Forsaken is a Pure who has been led astray by Changing Hag that is Luna. At any point, these lost wolves can be turned to a better path if they can be shown why they should renounce those &quot;gifts&quot; granted by the Moon.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, that requires beating some sense into their thick skulls. If you kill them, they can never convert. So hunt the Forsaken, show them why those &quot;gifts&quot; don't make them strong, take the territory they're too weak to hold in their dependence of a fickle goddess, but drive them out instead of killing them, so they will always have the opportunity to join the Pure as one People.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T13:06:09-07:00","id":1326325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326311#post1326311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not all Pure do. Even the 2E Core points out that there are some Pure who see murdering Forsaken as a wrong to be avoided. For example, take the perspective that every Forsaken is a Pure who has been led astray by Changing Hag that is Luna. At any point, these lost wolves can be turned to a better path if they can be shown why they should renounce those &quot;gifts&quot; granted by the Moon.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, that requires beating some sense into their thick skulls. If you kill them, they can never convert. So hunt the Forsaken, show them why those &quot;gifts&quot; don't make them strong, take the territory they're too weak to hold in their dependence of a fickle goddess, but drive them out instead of killing them, so they will always have the opportunity to join the Pure as one People.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Let's disregard how utterly fucked the Pure are if they won)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T13:08:03-07:00","id":1326326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326325#post1326325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Let's disregard how utterly fucked the Pure are if they won)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't. ^.^<br /> <br /> The Pure have a lot of issues with their operations, and I like the idea that they trade away a fickle mistress for worse gods closer to home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T13:14:28-07:00","id":1326327,"title":"","content":"I have to imagine there are some, even influential members of the Pure, who see that ripping down the Gauntlet is not the solution the more zealous think it is. Whether they're represented by the mysterious totems behind the Pure tribes, or the idea is reflected in the Firstborn totems of the Pure, remains to be seen. As it is you can run it any way you want.<br /> <br /> Digging the new Maeljin, really glad the way they went with Ghar'ma and Shad'ma. It is going to take me some time to get used to these names. I like the idea of Igsh'ma too, they would be killer as an antagonist that's big on the smashing.<br /> <br /> While we're relying on original creations for the Bale Hounds, maybe we'll get some symbols for them too, or for Viruhk-Ur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-20-2019, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T23:44:16-07:00","id":1326409,"title":"","content":"Observation - Is it consistent decision to mark every <b>Werewolf the Forsaken</b> 2E corebook reference as simply '<b>Werewolf the Forsaken</b>, p. XX' - instead of marking it's all about <b>WtF</b> 2E corebook? It was partially confusing to me, when starting to mark third errata like this - and then found out whole book is full of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T00:30:51-07:00","id":1326416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326409#post1326409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Observation - Is it consistent decision to mark every <b>Werewolf the Forsaken</b> 2E corebook reference as simply '<b>Werewolf the Forsaken</b>, p. XX' - instead of marking it's all about <b>WtF</b> 2E corebook? It was partially confusing to me, when starting to mark third errata like this - and then found out whole book is full of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be &quot;(see Werewolf: The Forsaken, p. XX)&quot; rather than any alternative. There's not really a need to state the edition when the current edition has been out for several years, as I doubt anyone will read this and instinctively check their first edition rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T00:32:37-07:00","id":1326417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326409#post1326409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Observation - Is it consistent decision to mark every <b>Werewolf the Forsaken</b> 2E corebook reference as simply '<b>Werewolf the Forsaken</b>, p. XX' - instead of marking it's all about <b>WtF</b> 2E corebook? It was partially confusing to me, when starting to mark third errata like this - and then found out whole book is full of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t understand what you\u2019re asking here, sorry.<br /> <br /> Edit: Having just read Matthew\u2019s response, are you honestly claiming confusion whether a 2e book with 2e branding on the front and back covers is referencing 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 07-21-2019, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T00:56:50-07:00","id":1326418,"title":"","content":"I don't understand all this chaos for Harmony. Its pretty clear: the pure respect their prey. Thats the only change. Oh yes and the people do not murder the people. And It has actually a lot of sense. They are still werewolves and still descendants of urfarah. They still have honor as renown and so on. Thats make them even more complicate and deep antagonists. They are prone to kill forsaken but they know that they must deal with the truth about harmony. Its probably the right price to pay to restore a world without traitors and moonslaves, for them.<br /> The fact that they are antagonists doesnt mean they haven't their own problems and struggles, individually. As every forsaken is not the same , also among the pure , is just immature ( and It can also lead to poor storytelling ) to think that all the ivory claws are nazi doctors and all the predator kings spend their time snapping forsaken necks and eating people alive. <br /> If the pure are still there and they are a serious problem is because they know how to deal with harmony. Also remember that with their tribal bans their harmony is probably even more easy to chance during the game. <br /> Also , with their kind of sacred prey, they probably have even a wider range of hunts. Nobody wrote &quot;the sacred prey of the pure are only the forsaken&quot;. And that is really important. <br /> The pure definitely know how to deal with harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 07-21-2019, 04:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T21:48:36-07:00","id":1326608,"title":"","content":"Reading Void Spirits section on 50th Anniversary of Moon Landing - So there are three types of Void Spirits presented in <b>Shunned</b>?<ul><li>Void Spirits proper - spirits of vacuum of space or light of distant stars</li> <li>Planetary angels - counterparts to Lunes and Helions from Mars, Jupiter and other Solar System planets. Get from them very 'alien invasion' vibe.</li> <li>Void Leviathans - great, cosmic colossus that are incomprehensible to other</li> </ul><br /> I'm not sure is first category is even a thing, text is a bit unclear there. ( Corrected - simple Void Spirits of vacuum of space are a thing, like example NPC shows)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-22-2019, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T23:31:51-07:00","id":1326629,"title":"","content":"After Void Spirits section I can wait for Dark Eras 2 'Golden Age of S-F' and possible 'War of Worlds' scenario with Martian Angels as invaders! \u2764\ufe0f","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-22-2019, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T17:50:08-07:00","id":1327306,"title":"","content":"so am I the only one reminded of FORT when reading RD-13? they seem VERY similar (and possibly make deviants)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T22:32:01-07:00","id":1327357,"title":"","content":"I remade few days ago my own fan chronicle antagonist - Fear of Scales - as Geryo, as I think it's more fitting. If anyone is interested how it would like - here it is. If want to comment - do it in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1137943-2e-fear-of-scales-\u2013-dragon-idigam?p=1326447#post1326447\">the original thread</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1137943-2e-fear-of-scales-\u2013-dragon-idigam?p=1326447#post1326447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is Fear of Scales as Geryo. I still need to imagine World Shaking effect for it.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fear of Scales as Geryo</span></b><br /> Geryo are First Children of Father Wolf. First mightiest predators that <i>Urfarah</i> unleashed on world of Pangea. Imperfect, flawed, unstable. Locked in Border Marches by their parent, left to die in new created Gauntlet. And Fear of Scales is probably first of them all. Scion of Wolf and Snake.<br /> <br /> When first Homo Sapiens found first great reptile in darkness, Fear of Scales was there. When man uncovered first dinosaur bones, telling stories of those impossible beasts \u2013 Fear of Scales was there. It was there, in darkness, waiting to slay new brave man to feed by their dedication. And it\u2019s waiting to this day. Releasing from its Gauntlet Lair by centuries apart, it hunts.<br /> <br /> Fear survived this long by two things \u2013 death and rebirth. Like a Snake it is spawn of, it \u2018shed the skin\u2019 and change itself, physically and metaphorically. Each time humans change their stories about mythical reptiles most of us known as dragons \u2013 it\u2019s Fear in its new form, feeding from stories of mortals. Can you really kill the story?<br /> <br /> <b>The Pray</b><br /> <br /> Fear of Scales is a creature of myths. Of stories. Like a literal dragon it is, it\u2019s main purpose is to test and defeat those that are destined to greatness. \u2018Heroes\u2019, as myths like to call them. It is not only to kill the would-be champion \u2013 but to test it, hare him, break him \u2013 and <i>then </i>kill him, before he become the savior of community, in his final decision. At least, that was from the time immemorial.<br /> <br /> With death of Father Wolf and creation of Gauntlet that become it\u2019s home \u2013 Fear has changed. It <i>evolved</i>. With death of <i>Urfarah</i>, it\u2019s natural role was broken. Era of true beasts and heroes is past. Only some petty humans and pesky werewolves. Fear evolved with the times it lived in. It started to look for next champions to be defeated and devoured, but cannot found any. So it\u2019s started to create them itself.<br /> <br /> When Sacred Hunt is calling Fear, it looks into \u2018River of Fate\u2019 and sense if someone has great destiny on itself. Someone who will become hero in near future \u2013 firefighter that by bravely will save family from burning building. Policeman that will stop murderer on duty. Attorney that will save the life of young child by pressing the charges. People that will achieve real good in future. And then Fear is hunting them, stealing their great future \u2013 and changing it to be struggle with ancient reptile monster. When the narrative of their life really change \u2013 Fear is reaping both the Essence of this struggle and meat of his hero-victim.<br /> <br /> Most will not survive more than one, two meetings with Fear. Like a cat playing with mouse, Fear feel it\u2019s not enough. So between calls of <i>Siskur-Dah</i>, it <b>creates</b> problems for future heroes to solve. Devouring corpses, poisoning the wells and lakes, stealing virgins \u2013 actions that will create chaos and make to act to solve them. In coming millennia, more and more Fear is dedicated to sowing the chaos than direct hunting people. Still, good meal is needed to have energy to plot next conspiracy \u2013 or something like that.<br /> <br /> Uratha here are twice good candidates for the \u2018heroes\u2019 Fear looks to devour. For one, they are race of scions from greatest predator and goddess of nearest sky planet. They are superb hunters. And Fate, in some weird coincidence, is favoring them as actors in greatest of universe plays. \u2018Children of two primordial parents, star crossed, one of that their children killed.\u2019 It\u2019s almost like Greek tragedy. If you find promising werewolf, it can easily become \u2018hero\u2019 Geryo need. Best are those that are blessed by Luna with some unfathomed destiny.<br /> <br /> Second, makes Uratha so delicious meal, is that they are \u2018correct\u2019 children of <i>Urfarah</i>. Fear was mistake in Father Wolf eyes. Werewolves are lucky ones, the beloved ones, the ones who came after and were considered complete. However, while killing Uratha is an indulgent pleasure, it is the slow dwindle, the cruel defeat, that truly satisfy Fear. It prefers to bring a werewolf low, to mire the prey in his own failings and slowly tear away the foundations of his world, then leave him to despair amid the wreckage \u2014 possibly infected with the Geryo strain.<br /> <br /> When not actively on the Hunt, Fear is in it\u2019s Lair in Gauntlet Realm, rarely staying longer in similar small Lairs in Flesh or Spirit, however its hunting or planning to flush up. Lesser Lairs are its Spawn and local Heralds meeting places for plotting and kidnaping would-be heroes or their \u2018saved ones\u2019.<br /> <br /> <b>Servants</b><br /> <br /> Being mythical Dragon, Fear of Scales likes to use his own Spawn as lesser minions. To represent the story it\u2019s created in each iteration, it choose human or werewolf Herald that plays a role of \u2018sole survivor of Dragon\u2019s attack\u2019 in alarming next community First want to test. Fear then consumes generated Essence by the doubt this news makes in community.<br /> <br /> <b>Description</b><br /> <br /> Fear of Scales do not hides it nature when confronted. It\u2019s assume the most popular image of dragon in particular times \u2013 in the end, stories of its terrible deeds are sustaining it by eons now - but it\u2019s always reptilian horror being, sending fear in the hearts of human and werewolves. In Vikings Era it could resemble mythical Nidhogg \u2013 this form is a long, serpentine being gliding in the air that spread acid on the ground and have taste for human corpses. In high Middle Ages, it can be classical foul reptilian beast of Saint George - with scales and great wings. Only real common points are its size \u2013 about of great plane \u2013 and it\u2019s reptilian features.<br /> <br /> Fear can shapechange body parts of it into lesser beings \u2013 like one of four legs or his heads \u2013 and send them as his avatars, in physical disguise. However, most of the time it much more like to choose it\u2019s Heralds and his Spawn as much more suited to long term infiltration missions than real parts of itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Killing Form</b><br /> <br /> All First can assume Killing Form, <i>Gauru </i>equivalent for Geryo, often with multiple limbs or body parts. Fear is very simple in it\u2019s Form \u2013 it has three heads and great wings. Legends say that each head is looking into other realm \u2013 Flesh, Shadow and Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://previews.123rf.com/images/fotokostic/fotokostic1406/fotokostic140600055/29391956-illustration-of-three-headed-dragon.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Rumors</b><br /> <br /> Some rumors points that Geryo <b><i>Orocheiros</i></b> ( see <b>Shunned by the Moon</b> ) is latest incarnation of <i>Fear of Scales</i>. Others that they are simply related by common parentage.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stats</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Fear of Scales</span></b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 5<br /> <b>Blood:</b> Sadistic<br /> <b>Bone:</b> Testing<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 15, Finesse 14, Resistance 13<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 50<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 27<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 14<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 29<br /> <b>Size:</b> 30<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 43 (73)<br /> <b>World Shaking:</b> ???<br /> <b>Gifts:</b> (Death) All; (Dominance) All; (Hunger) All; (Insight) All; (Weather) All<br /> <b>Dread Powers</b>: Burrow, Colossus, Dragonfire, Forge Servant (Herald, Spawn)<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Fear of Scales must follow the taboo of the story it now recreates with its victim. Most often it\u2019s need to eat people willingly sacrificing for others. Fear then need to leave this community for at least year and one day.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> The bones of a human who possessed an Integrity rating of 10 when they died. In medieval times, this person would be called saint.<br /> <br /> <b>New Dread Power - <i>Dragonfire </i></b><br /> (Based on the same called Atavism <b>from Beast: The Primodrial</b> )<br /> First can blast area with gouts of fire. This counts as a ranged area attack on his Rank radius circle and requires a roll of Geryo\u2019s Power + Finesse. Beings in area can use Dodge action to counter this if they do not use any action in this turn. Damage from blast is Aggravated and adds First\u2019s Rank as a weapon modifier. Flammable materials ignite on contact, turning the area into a raging inferno if it is not contained quickly. Then again, that may be the point. Dragonfire ignores Durability equal to the Geryo\u2019s Rank dots. Furthermore, fire causes no damage to First, and it never suffers environmental penalties or damage caused by heat and smoke, which are like clear air to it.<br /> <br /> <b>Alternative Dread Power \u2013 <i>Colossus</i></b><br /> If possible use of <b>Storypath</b> corebooks, instead of adding extra Size Health and modifying Armour for being, assume that Colossus being has Scale equal to its Rank and normal people have Scale 1. Uratha in Gauru and similar changers have Scale rise up by 1, so Scale 2 to comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T11:43:59-07:00","id":1328340,"title":"","content":"The more I think about it, the Crazy Rumor Guy for the Void Spirits\u2019 has a point: what DID Luna do with Gaia\u2019s hateful little shits( Or uncommonly, planetary angels)?<br /> <br /> Now the instant gratification part of my brain wants to go: MAKE THE GM ANGELS GAIAS ANGELS DO IT DO IT DO IT DO IT<br /> <br /> But the thinking part of my brain has come up with a theory: what if the Idigam were once Gaia\u2019s servants, but Luna/ Helios/ The God-Machine/ Exarches put her into Slumber, and that in turn the proto Idigam lost connection to their progenitor/ analogue, thus they devolved into formless chaos \u2014 ripe to be hunted down and imprisoned?<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll admit it\u2019s not very plausible, but Tons of entities that break conventions when it comes to What spirits are and are not capable of doing, so so I think it would be an interesting possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-30-2019, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T12:03:26-07:00","id":1328346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1326283#post1326283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 2) The Khorne of CofD would be Asmodai who wants blood for blood's sake, Thurifuge is the Architect of Violence. The one who feeds from institutionalized violence, the one who feed from the engineering act that was the so called Final Solution, or the infrastructure put forward in the prosecution of wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be more specific, Asmodai is the Queen of Wrath, but it needn\u2019t be just spur of the moment bloodshed. Oh no, ice cold revenge and elaborate plots to get back at those who have hurt you are just as good to Her.<br /> <br /> And despite his Title, Thurifuge is actually far more fond of sporadic, aimless violence than institutionalized conflict; it empowers him far more regularly than warfare. Remember, all violence is under His purview. While he still greatly enjoys warfare and the pain it brings, there\u2019s really nothing like the Essence produced by the jaded rich brat who sets a homeless man on Fire because he felt like he could. That\u2019s something to be encouraged and propagated in Thurifuge\u2019s eyes. Bloody or not, grandly conducted genocide or a minor spur of the moment decision to kick a guy you dislike in the nuts and then curb stomp him into unconsciousness; Thurifuge cherishes it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T12:43:38-07:00","id":1328357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1328340#post1328340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the thinking part of my brain has come up with a theory: what if the Idigam were once Gaia\u2019s servants, but Luna/ Helios/ The God-Machine/ Exarches put her into Slumber, and that in turn the proto Idigam lost connection to their progenitor/ analogue, thus they devolved into formless chaos \u2014 ripe to be hunted down and imprisoned?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've also thought about that options, considering the fact that a) as the idigam do not lose Essence in the Shadow (unlike regular spirits) they seem to be more naturally tuned to Hisil, hinting about them being its &quot;original inhabitants&quot; and b) that following Chris Allens' writeup for &quot;spirit nobles&quot; and the similarity between their capabilities and the idigam's natural abilities (that is, their common ability to influence/ shape their surroundings and servants), making them possibly the &quot;original nobility&quot; of the Shadow. And considering that Gaia may very well <i>be</i> Earth's Shadow, having such strong connection to Hisil means a similarly strong connection to Gaia- so they may very well be Gaia's original &quot;planetary angels&quot;... other from the fact that following the only idigam example in Sundered World, and the Earthbound which have never been banished from the world, it doesn't seem like being detached from Gaia caused their devolution (unless you consider Gaia being asleep as enough detachment to cause them to turn formless- and them I must ask about the awakening state of Mars, Uranus, Pluto and other stellar spirits).<br /> <br /> Another possibility for &quot;Gaia's angels&quot; could be the pangaean of course (Pangaea, Gaea/Gaia, close enough)... or, of course, <i>the actual spirits we all know</i>. I mean, what are the spirits of Hisil of not the actual spirits of Earth's Shadow and its inhabitants?.. except of the fact that, like I said above, spirits do not seem to have a strong connection to Hisil like other Ephemerals have with their realms (ghosts excluded, but that's part of the point). I mean, if the Spirits of the Shadow are <i>not</i> Gaia's angels and emanations- <i>then what in the name of Urfarah are they?</i><br /> <br /> (yeah, I understand that it likely involves humans in some way, see ghosts as reference, but how and why?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T14:42:34-07:00","id":1328386,"title":"","content":"Elaborate revenge, the successful examples of, are engineered. Ergo, Thurifuge.<br /> <br /> That brat who set the homeless man on fire? There's nothing random about it. Accelerants were produced, sold and bought for that express purpose. But I digress. Check out Lore of the Forsaken or Blasphemies if you want to disagree with me further. The one who skewed the system to allow for such disparities in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T21:59:35-07:00","id":1328451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1328386#post1328386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elaborate revenge, the successful examples of, are engineered. Ergo, Thurifuge.<br /> <br /> That brat who set the homeless man on fire? There's nothing random about it. Accelerants were produced, sold and bought for that express purpose. But I digress. Check out Lore of the Forsaken or Blasphemies if you want to disagree with me further. The one who skewed the system to allow for such disparities in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Lore of the Forsaken was what I was referencing, not sure why you think I\u2019m disagreeing with you. Merely pointing out that he is is the Maeljin of Violence in its entirety, and is empowered by more than pre meditated murder. He can be fed through animals preying on each other after all, human malice just grants him greater power.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t forget, the other Maeljin inadvertently grant him power through their own schemes more often than not too, and He takes all the credit like the jerk that he rightfully is xD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-31-2019, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-10T12:12:37-07:00","id":1334921,"title":"","content":"I got my hardcopy, nice sized book, and its so worth it. Thanks everyone involved!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-10-2019, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T11:27:17-07:00","id":1335165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1323454-shunned-by-the-moon-is-on-dtrpg?p=1328357#post1328357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've also thought about that options, considering the fact that a) as the idigam do not lose Essence in the Shadow (unlike regular spirits) they seem to be more naturally tuned to Hisil, hinting about them being its &quot;original inhabitants&quot; and b) that following Chris Allens' writeup for &quot;spirit nobles&quot; and the similarity between their capabilities and the idigam's natural abilities (that is, their common ability to influence/ shape their surroundings and servants), making them possibly the &quot;original nobility&quot; of the Shadow. And considering that Gaia may very well <i>be</i> Earth's Shadow, having such strong connection to Hisil means a similarly strong connection to Gaia- so they may very well be Gaia's original &quot;planetary angels&quot;... other from the fact that following the only idigam example in Sundered World, and the Earthbound which have never been banished from the world, it doesn't seem like being detached from Gaia caused their devolution (unless you consider Gaia being asleep as enough detachment to cause them to turn formless- and them I must ask about the awakening state of Mars, Uranus, Pluto and other stellar spirits).<br /> <br /> Another possibility for &quot;Gaia's angels&quot; could be the pangaean of course (Pangaea, Gaea/Gaia, close enough)... or, of course, <i>the actual spirits we all know</i>. I mean, what are the spirits of Hisil of not the actual spirits of Earth's Shadow and its inhabitants?.. except of the fact that, like I said above, spirits do not seem to have a strong connection to Hisil like other Ephemerals have with their realms (ghosts excluded, but that's part of the point). I mean, if the Spirits of the Shadow are <i>not</i> Gaia's angels and emanations- <i>then what in the name of Urfarah are they?</i><br /> <br /> (yeah, I understand that it likely involves humans in some way, see ghosts as reference, but how and why?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First... GM = Gaia Machine. *runs away cackling!*<br /> <br /> Ehem. Ok, now that that's done, let's speculate:<br /> <br /> The Hisil contains the spiritual reflection of living things, or of concepts that are given reality by living things. These living things includes plants and animals, which do not have souls and as such their spiritual reflections reside in the Hisil. Humanity does have souls (for whatever reason) and as such the spirits of humans don't go far and effectively &quot;claim&quot; human flesh. (Thus a human claimed by another spirit is effectively a magath, explaining why they look/act so warped.)<br /> <br /> But we can't say that living things explains the Hisil, because there are demonstrably spirits present from places that are not &quot;alive&quot; in a traditional sense. Thus the equation is flipped: that which has spirit (not &quot;a spirit) is alive, and the observed deadness of the world when separated from the Hisil is explained.<br /> <br /> Gaia itself may be defined as the Earth's planetary spirit, which would be a presence in the Hisil except that she is sleeping. Thus we cannot say that Gaia IS the Earth's shadow, but could say that the Earth is alive because it has a spiritual reflection in a (slumbering) Gaia.<br /> <br /> Postulate: Gaia was put to sleep because if she had stayed awake no other, more complex life could have taken root--it would have been consumed immediately, as that is the nature of the Hisil itself. Further, the &quot;putting to sleep&quot; was orchestrated by Helios with the help of Theia/Luna. Luna is the Warden Moon, but it's not there to ward the Earth from the rest of the solar system, it's there to pin Gaia into the universe's longest nap, a cosmic jailor of an entity that would destroy the complex panalopy of life she and Helios have enabled.<br /> <br /> Now thing is, Luna gets farther from Gaia every year, and the very act that knocked Gaia into sleep left so much of Theia lost inside her--and so much of Gaia lost inside Theia--that both could be called planetary Magath. &quot;Luna&quot; has never been quite right since....<br /> <br /> If this is sufficiently correct, and the Idigam are Gaia's planetary angels, then it could explain why they went to sleep on Luna instead of, oh, being devoured by her?<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}